Driverpackage for STM32H7xx
===========================

CPU-Family: STM32H7xx
--------------------------------------------------------------

CPU-typ
-------
STM32H743x


Hardware
--------
Nucleo-H743ZI
CPU-clock (PLL): 400MHz
Timer: SysTick


Compiler
--------
Keil ARMCC v5.26.0 / Workbench µVision5.


Timer
-----
1kHz (1ms)


CAN Clock (APB1)
---------
80MHz


CAN1-Pins
--------
RX: PD0
TX: PD1

CAN2-Pins
--------
RX: PB5
TX: PB6

USART3 (APB1)
------
RxD: PD9
TxD: PD8
115200Baud 8N1

Notes:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.
Debug output ( printf() ) is optional possible. The output is routed to USART3 (BaudRate=115200). 
The compiler switch "CONFIG_NO_PRINTF" is set in the driver file examples.h.
If this define is set no printf output is generated. (default setting)
2.
The driver used the STM-HAL STM32Cube_FW_H7_V1.7.0 from the STM32CubeH7 Firmware Package.
Before you can build and run the examples, 
please download the firmware package from the ST websites and copy it into the driver folder (../driver/stm32_h7).
In the example projects the include paths to this STM32CubeH7 Firmware package are relatively created.
e.g.:  
..\..\..\drivers\stm32_h7\STM32Cube_FW_H7_V1.7.0\Drivers\STM32H7xx_HAL_Driver\Inc

That means the compiler is looking for the package right there.
